Z||000000||Ralfy9862||10-05-2000||10:26 AM||||when i start my car a noise goes on for a little while . What is it its not any of my belt or the transmision so i have no idea . Anybody know<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||stsmithgt||10-05-2000||10:43 AM||||I had a squeak or more like a whistle when I started my car and the noise would go away in a few minutes.  It turned out to be the gasket under my air cleaner housing.  It was made of paper and pretty much decomposed.  I replaced it with a rubber one I made and the noise is gone. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Just a strange option it possibly could be.||||reg||1
Z||000002||tgowens||10-05-2000||11:23 AM||||It is probably the alternator belt. It is a common problem in the Fiero and we see it here all the time at the Fiero Shop. You might want to either tighten your alternator belt by loosening the bottom bolt on the bracket and repositioning the alternator to tighten the belt or replace the belt (in wich case you will need to tighten the alternator anyway)...<P>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/tgowens_sig.gif">                        <BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A> - Blue '87 GT - Gold '87 GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||RiceCooker||10-05-2000||02:46 PM||||The Waterpump sqeuaks on startup if your bearings have failed. Keep an eye out for any coolant leaks.||||reg||1
Z||000004||contra||10-05-2000||08:30 PM||||i had a squeek<BR>thought it was my belts<BR>so i changed my A/C belt and my alternator belt. But then my fiero decided to throw up and spit on me when i got my paycheque. My water pump exploded or died and antifreeze was pouring out.<BR>got it all fixed at once for a hundred bucks<BR>which isn't bad cause i dunno how to do all that work in those tight spaces  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||DXR_DAD||10-05-2000||11:50 PM||||I say water pump, DO NOT OVER TIGHTEN THE BELT, the old water pump won't like it!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>It's not that hard to replace, just did one a month or so ago. Most of the time the belt is a loud squeak, and you know what it is, also when the belt is wet you will get the same noise (squeak)<P><BR>DXR_DAD||||reg||1
